# Implementations — Rhyme-SHAKE

## Directory Structure

```
Implementations/
├── Reference_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-128/   (portable C99, SHAKE backend)
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-384/
│   └── Rhyme-SHAKE-512/
├── Optimized_Implementation/
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-128/   (-march=native, DP1 fast-keygen target)
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-256/
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-384/
│   ├── Rhyme-SHAKE-512/
│   └── README
├── Additional_Implementation/
│   └── README
└── README
```

## Reference_Implementation

Portable C99, `-DRHYME_NO_AES`.  Hash/XOF: SHAKE-128/256 via `fips202.c`.
Wrapper layer: `rhyme_xof.c/h`.

## Optimized_Implementation

`-O3 -march=native`.  Two targets:

| Target | Binary | KAT vs Reference |
|--------|--------|-----------------|
| `make` | `KAT_SIG` | byte-identical |
| `make fast` | `KAT_SIG_FAST` | differs (DP1, valid) |

DP1 uses a truncated-minor coprimality check for ~8-14x faster keygen
at higher security levels.  All signatures self-verify.

## Common Files

`api.h` — public API parameters
`SIG_AlgorithmInstance.c/h` — API_PKC SIG wrapper
`KAT_SIG.c` — KAT driver
`auxfunc.c/h`, `drng.c/h` — API_PKC no-modify files (byte-identical to template)
`rhyme_xof.c/h` — Rhyme-specific Hash/XOF wrappers
`include/` — public headers
`src/` — core algorithm implementation
